ularly in the  warmer climates i mean there's so much  conflicting information i can't make  head or tail of it what i do know is  that the people  probably people on both sides are  completely unreasonable that the people  who are pushing the panic button  are out falsifying information  they treat anyone who disagrees with  them as a a heretic  uh  you know very much reminiscent of the  kind of uh atmosphere that there was in  in the totalitarian  germany or or you know stalin is russia  there's only one party line anyone who  disagrees with it is evil  uh to be eliminated and the ends justify  the means and and and certainly within  the sort of uh  the global warming  um  tribe  there's a lot of the sort of  anti-capitalism anti-west it's bad  industrialism is you know  industrialization is bad and i don't buy  any of that and of course inevitably  there's a lot of these sort of  anti-capitalist anti-globalization  people demonstrating and making a big  nuisance of themselves i mean the fact  of the matter is as i've said before  here we live much better today than we  ever did before everywhere  including in the underdeveloped world  the proof is that there's so many people  living there you know  yeah we have altered the ecosystem we  have altered in a way that favors humans  because it used to be that maybe there  are only a million people living on the  planet a million humans another seven  billion so something there must be good  for humans or there wouldn't be seven  billion of them and there are these  extreme environmentalists who say that  that's bad for the planet well i don't  care i mean the planet will survive the  planet will adapt you know uh  we have a situation in british columbia  where there's a massive attack of the  mountain pine beetle  well that's bad for the trees  bad for the forest industry but it's  good for the mountain pine beetle  they're doing really well and as they  have periodically in the past although  some people are saying it's caused by  global warming well then why did the  outbreak take place in the north and  it's now moving south  uh you know where it's warmer it started  where it was colder  i don't know whatever happens to the  environment it'll benefit some species  and not other species my interest in  thing is in things that benefit the  human species obviously in the long term  not in the short term  and i think  that we could finesse the whole issue  if we simply address the fact that we  shouldn't be depleting non-renewable  resources when there are renewable  resources available why aren't we  burning all the garbage to make power  there's a tremendous amount of  biomass out there but it's not  economical to use it so obviously the  price of energy needs to be raised and i  don't believe the alarm is to say that  that will cost millions of jobs and  cause our um economy to come to a  grinding grinding halt it didn't happen  when oil went from five dollars a barrel  to 50.  so let's just double the price of  electricity we'll have to pay more for  it but then it'll be bring on a lot of  renewable energy resources and maybe  make wind power more economical and  solar and a number of other things and  stop arguing back and forth about  global warming and pretending and hiding  information to justify this position or  that position it's just i mean i'm in  the forest industry we plant trees we  plant trees not because we think it's it  costs money to plant trees and tend the  forest  but and and there's no return on it i  can't justify it i'm not going to be  here we live in we operate in the  northern boreal forest the trees take 90  years to grow  i won't be here in 90 years and if i  thought of investing money for 90 years  i wouldn't plant trees because i have no  idea what they're going to do with trees  in 90 years from now it's just a cost we  take trees out we put trees back in so  there should be some kind of attacks on  non-renewable energy usage  another agenda here at in this  copenhagen conference is the whole idea  that somehow the west is bad because  they have caused the problem of co2  emissions but the fact the matter is  that the population in the third world  has grown  tremendously this past century has grown  much faster than in the bad west and  it's done so because of the kind of  technology and the kind of medical uh  you know advances that have  come out of out of this the  industrialized world  which no longer is just the west because  japan is very much part of the  industrialized world so is korea so are  parts of china and parts of other  countries parts of the middle east parts  of africa and so forth  and you know we will find ways to live  within  the means of the resources that that we  have available to us we used to have 80  of the people on the farm and now it's  like three percent in the developed  world and they produce too much in the  way of agricultural products  uh the whole idea that somehow the west  now owes it to the developing countries  i don't buy that it's like this whole  thing about the africans trying to claim  compensation for slavery i mean get  serious i i don't know i did in  tremendous detail but i suspected what  happened when the europeans went to  africa they went there looking for trade  and so what are they going to trade  they're going to trade what the local  market has to offer  and in indonesia spices in africa it was  slaves why were slaves available it's  not because the europeans went charging  around the jungle looking for slaves  it's because that was the product that  the local merchants were offering them  because slavery wasn't invented by the  bad western colonialists slavery has  been around since the beginning of time  and as long as there were wars people  were taking  slaves and trading them and it was a  commodity in those days and those were  the values that prevailed at that time  and it was the west that put a stop to  slavery and long after that slavery  continued in the ottoman empire and in  the arab world and in many other places  so  i mean history is history things happen  one group beats up on another group not  very nice uh in  all continents in latin what used to be  i mean mesoamerica different groups were  at war with each other taking slaves it  was the same in africa in asia  so i i think that this whole  anti-western  anti-capitalist agenda that seems to be  bound into the whole global warming  thing doesn't help the cause but it's an  opportunity people jump on this just  like al gore is making all kinds of  money uh pretending to be a profit of of  greenism  and this whole cap and trade thing is  going to spawn a whole group of  profiteers are going to jump on this  just like those bankers devising all  kinds of clever schemes  to parasite off money that other people  generate with with genuinely productive  enterprises so  my take on all of this is it's just  another example of  all these bureaucrats living high off  the hog traveling around the world  that we should finesse the whole thing  by saying we shouldn't be depleting  non-renewable energy resources and you  know that's not only good green uh  philosophy it's good for my business  because i'm in the wood business so use  more wood capture carbon in your  buildings with lumber  let us use biomass to make energy raise  the price of electricity and that's it  for now thank you
 

